# ADR-317 backup and policy evaluation

Measured locally on 2026-08-23 with `scripts/run-adr317-evaluation.sh` and an
isolated live backup/rotation/restore drill.

| Check | Result |
|---|---|
| Labeled corpus split | 2 train, 2 calibration |
| Style confusion | TP 1, TN 3, FP 0, FN 0 |
| Channel contribution | surface and grammar reported for sustained drift |
| Rewrite percentile | required channels reduced from 100 to 0 in fixture |
| Protected values | name, number, negation, and speaker preserved |
| Changed values | removed name, number, and negation detected |
| Near-copy gate | 16-grapheme owner-corpus match classified manual-only |
| Attempt bound | 1 to 20 attempts, enforced by `StyleAnalysisJob` |
| Finding cooldown | 5 minutes to 30 days; default 24 hours |
| Live backup | encrypted online snapshot passed integrity checks |
| Key rotation | new artifact decrypted byte-identically; old key rejected |
| Isolated restore | integrity, migration, counts, replay, and render hashes passed |

The detailed machine-readable report is generated at
`artifacts/evaluations/ADR-317.json`. Backup encryption-key rotation and the
separate access-token pepper-loss/reissue procedure are documented in
`docs/operations/backup-and-restore.md`.
